---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Upwork Proposal Kit | Redefining Retirement"
  description="An easy way to dip your toe into freelancing and consulting after 50. Inside: a cover letter you can actually use, the messages I send once a client replies, a way to find adjacent work, and the prompt I'd paste into an agent today."
  type="article"
  noindex={true}
  bare={true}
>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">

      <header class="article-header">
        <p class="issue-stamp">The Upwork Proposal Kit · Subscriber Edition</p>
        <h1 class="article-title">Upwork Proposal Kit</h1>
        <p class="article-deck">An easy way to dip your toe into freelancing and consulting after 50. Inside: a cover letter you can actually use, the messages I send once a client replies, a way to find adjacent work, and the prompt I'd paste into an agent today.</p>
        <p class="byline">By Corey Koehler · Redefining Retirement · Class of '90</p>
      </header>

      <div class="hello-section">
        <img
          src="/images/corey-portrait.jpg"
          alt="Corey Koehler"
          class="hello-photo"
          onerror="this.style.display='none'"
        />
        <div class="hello-text">
          <h2>Hello</h2>
          <p>Hey, I'm Corey Koehler.</p>
          <p>Foundry worker. Then 17 years behind a CAD station as a mechanical draftsman. Then midlife solopreneur.</p>
          <p>I've been on Upwork for years, back when it was still called Elance. A lot of my clients have come from there.</p>
          <p>This kit is what I'd hand a friend who wanted to test freelancing or consulting after 50. No promises that Upwork will work for you, or that an AI agent will land you clients. Just a letter, a prompt, and a plain way to start the conversation.</p>
          <p>Let's get into it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <nav class="contents" aria-label="Contents">
        <p class="result-section-label">Contents</p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href="#start-here-freelancing-after-50-on-upwork">Start here: freelancing after 50 on Upwork</a></li>
          <li><a href="#the-2026-conversational-cover-letter-upwork-proposal-template">The 2026 conversational cover letter (Upwork proposal template)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-i-handle-a-potential-client-on-upwork">How I handle a potential client on Upwork</a></li>
          <li><a href="#look-for-adjacent-work-on-upwork">Look for adjacent work on Upwork</a></li>
          <li><a href="#dont-shy-away-from-teach-me-jobs-on-upwork">Don't shy away from teach-me jobs on Upwork</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-should-i-charge-on-upwork">What should I charge on Upwork?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-service-should-i-offer-as-a-freelancer-after-50">What service should I offer as a freelancer after 50?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#the-ai-proposal-prompt-for-upwork">The AI proposal prompt for Upwork</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-id-use-an-agent-with-the-official-upwork-connector-mcp">How I'd use an agent with the official Upwork connector (MCP)</a></li>
          <li><a href="#what-top-upwork-educators-say-about-writing-a-proposal-plus-my-own-tactics">What top Upwork educators say about writing a proposal, plus my own tactics</a></li>
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <section class="kit-section" id="start-here-freelancing-after-50-on-upwork">
        <h2>Start here: freelancing after 50 on Upwork</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Freelancing and consulting make a good first business after 50.</p>
          <p>You already have skills someone will pay for. Or you can learn one narrow skill without building a whole company around it first.</p>
          <p>You can start small, on your own schedule. You find out if you even like the work before you rearrange the rest of your life.</p>
          <p>That's the whole point of dipping a toe in. You're not launching a store. You're not hiring a staff. You're testing a way to get paid for what you already know how to do.</p>
          <p>Upwork is a simple place to run that test. The jobs are already posted. The payments stay on the platform. You send a short proposal, have a conversation, and see if it's a fit.</p>
          <p>What's in here: a cover letter you can actually use, a prompt you can paste into Grok Bot or another agent, and a plain look at how I'd use Upwork's new official connector if I were setting this up today.</p>
          <p>Here's what I'd do first.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="step-list">
          <li>Write down two or three kinds of work you already do well. Keep it plain. "I can set up a simple newsletter." "I can run Google Ads for a small shop." "I can clean up a messy WordPress site." Then list the tools and platforms around those skills, not just the skill name. There's a simple method for that later in this kit.</li>
          <li>Make a short Knowledge Section for yourself. Your skills, the years or examples you can stand behind, and any testimonial you have permission to use. If you're new, say so, and point to the experience you do have.</li>
          <li>Use the 2026 cover letter template in this kit. Keep it to about 200 to 300 words. Lead with the client's words, not your bio.</li>
          <li>Want help with the first draft? Paste the AI prompt into Grok Bot or another agent, then paste the job post. Edit before you send anything.</li>
          <li>If you connect Upwork's official agent connector, let it help you search and draft. You still confirm every proposal. Connects are only spent when you say yes.</li>
          <li>When a client replies, stay in Upwork Messages until there's a contract. Use the client-handling notes later in this kit as a starting point. Then rewrite them so they sound like you.</li>
        </ol>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>You don't need a new website, a logo, or a six-month plan to try this.</p>
        </aside>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Want the slower, fuller picture of starting on Upwork after 50, including whether it's even a fit for you? I wrote that here: <a href="https://redefiningretirement.io/p/start-a-business-at-50-freelancing-on-upwork">Freelance on Upwork After 50</a>.</p>
          <p>Stuck on what to charge, or what service to offer? I already wrote those up too: <a href="https://redefiningretirement.io/p/gen-xers-worth-freelancer-upwork">how Gen Xers can find their worth on Upwork</a>, and <a href="https://redefiningretirement.io/p/unique-way-get-ideas-start-business-50-using-google">how to use Google and free tools to find in-demand services at 50</a>. The short versions, plus the videos, are later in this kit.</p>
          <p>This kit is the proposal part. A simple way to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="kit-section" id="the-2026-conversational-cover-letter-upwork-proposal-template">
        <h2>The 2026 conversational cover letter (Upwork proposal template)</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>I've been rewriting this letter, off and on, since 2013, back in the Elance days. The old version was longer. It also invited people to book a Zoom on my calendar.</p>
          <p>That last part doesn't belong in a proposal anymore. Upwork wants the conversation to stay on the platform until a contract starts. The idea is the same: talk to the client soon. The channel is now Upwork Messages.</p>
          <p>A few other things changed too. Most letters should land around 200 to 300 words. Every proposal costs Connects. And I don't open with "Hello from Minnesota" anymore. "Hello," works fine. So does "Hello [Name]," if you can find the name.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>In the results list, clients only see the first two lines of your letter. Plus your name, photo, badges, rate, and Job Success Score.</p>
        </aside>

        <h3 class="block-title">The template</h3>
        <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
          <div class="tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Cover letter template">
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="letter-tab-1" aria-controls="letter-panel-1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">The letter</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="letter-tab-2" aria-controls="letter-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Optional P.S.</button>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="letter-panel-1" aria-labelledby="letter-tab-1" class="is-active" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">The letter</h3>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">The template</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Hello [Name],

I can help you [the task, using the client's exact words].

You mentioned [one specific detail from the post]. I've done similar work, including [one relevant result I can actually stand behind]. I would start by [a simple first step].

If you're open to a short conversation this week, we can do it through Upwork Messages. A video call in the thread works too.

I guarantee you'll get useful, specific suggestions from that conversation. If you don't, I'll donate $20 to the charity of your choice.

[Your name]

From past clients (optional, only with permission, and only if they match this job):

"[Short quote.]" - [First name, or "a recent client"]</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="letter-panel-2" aria-labelledby="letter-tab-2" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Optional P.S.</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>New to this category on Upwork? If that's actually true, you can add this P.S.:</p>
            </div>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Only if it is true</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>P.S. I'm fairly new to this category on Upwork, so I'm willing to do the first milestone at 50% off my regular rate. Any later work is at my regular rate if we continue.</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>Don't tack that P.S. onto every bid out of habit. And don't offer it if it isn't true.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="block-title">How to fill it in</h3>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Line 1 is "Hello [Name]," if the name is in the post, or in a review you can actually see. Otherwise, just "Hello,".</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>Don't invent a name.</p>
        </aside>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Line 2 has to work as a preview. Use the client's own words for the work they want done. "I can help you redesign the checkout page so fewer people abandon their cart" beats "I am a highly experienced designer."</p>
          <p>The next paragraph proves you read the post. One observation, one relevant result, one simple first step.</p>
          <p>No matching result? Don't make one up. Show you understood the job, and be honest about what you've done.</p>
          <p>Then invite a conversation in Upwork Messages. No Calendly link, personal Zoom link, email, phone number, LinkedIn profile, or website with a contact form.</p>
          <p>The $20 charity guarantee is on by default in the template and the prompt, because I still use it in my own letters. Delete it if it doesn't sound like you.</p>
          <p>Sign with your name only.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="note">
          <p class="note-label">Note</p>
          <p>Answer every screening question in its own box. Attach a sample that matches this job, if you have one. If a job asks for an Uma video interview instead of a cover letter, don't force this template into that slot.</p>
        </aside>

        <h3 class="block-title">After they say yes</h3>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Once the client messages you, the work shifts to the conversation. Stay in Upwork Messages until a contract is in place. Still no Calendly link, personal Zoom link, email, phone number, or LinkedIn profile.</p>
          <p>The messages below are the kind I send, or would send, in that thread. Don't paste them word for word. Change the wording so it sounds like you.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>Clients can spot a canned reply a mile away.</p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section class="kit-section" id="how-i-handle-a-potential-client-on-upwork">
        <h2>How I handle a potential client on Upwork</h2>
        <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
          <div class="tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Client scripts">
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-1" aria-controls="script-panel-1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">They reply</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-2" aria-controls="script-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Discovery call</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-3" aria-controls="script-panel-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Scoping</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-4" aria-controls="script-panel-4" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">The quote</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-5" aria-controls="script-panel-5" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">A polite no</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="script-tab-6" aria-controls="script-panel-6" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Follow-up</button>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-1" aria-labelledby="script-tab-1" class="is-active" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Reply when they show interest</h3>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Change the wording so it sounds like you</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Hello [first name],

Thanks for getting back to me. Glad this looks like it could be a fit.

I have a few questions so I can scope this properly. I'm also happy to hop on a short call right here in Upwork Messages if that's easier. The phone icon in this thread starts a Zoom or voice call, so everything stays on the platform.

What times work for you this week?

[Your name]</pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-2" aria-labelledby="script-tab-2" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Invite a discovery call inside Upwork</h3>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Change the wording so it sounds like you</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Hello [first name],

Thanks for being open to a conversation.

We can do a short Zoom or voice call right in Upwork Messages (the phone icon in this thread). Reply with a couple of times that work for you this week. Once we pick one, I'll send the call invite through Upwork.

Looking forward to talking.

[Your name]</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>Once a contract is in place, you can use your own calendar or Zoom if you want. Not before.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-3" aria-labelledby="script-tab-3" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Scoping questions</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>Maybe they'd rather stay in chat. Or maybe you want a little context before the call. Either way, keep the questions short and specific.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Ask only what you actually need</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Before we jump on a call, or if you'd rather handle this in messages, here's what would help me quote this accurately:

1. What does "done" look like for you?
2. Is there a deadline I should know about?
3. What have you already tried, if anything?
4. Who will I be working with, and how should we check in?
5. Is this a one-time project, or are you hoping it turns into ongoing help?

No need to write a novel. A few sentences on each is plenty.</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>Ask only what you actually need. If the job post already answered a question, don't ask it again just to pad the list.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-4" aria-labelledby="script-tab-4" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">A quote or next-step message</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>Send this after you understand the work. Not before.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Change the wording so it sounds like you</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Thanks for the conversation, [first name].

Based on what you described, here's how I'd approach it: [two or three plain steps].

For this scope, my quote is [amount] for [what's included], with [a realistic timeline]. If you want to start, I can send a contract through Upwork. The first milestone would be [the first piece of work].

If anything in the scope should change, tell me and I'll adjust the quote before we start.

[Your name]</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>Send the official offer or contract through Upwork. Don't move payment off the platform.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-5" aria-labelledby="script-tab-5" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">A polite decline</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>Say no when you're not the right fit. It beats stretching or going quiet.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Change the wording so it sounds like you</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Thanks for thinking of me for this, [first name].

After reading it through, I don't think I'm the right person for [the honest reason: the timeline, the type of work, or that this is not work I do]. I'd rather tell you now than waste your time.

I hope you find the right person quickly.

[Your name]</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>You don't owe them a referral. If you really do know someone who's a better fit, and you're comfortable saying so, mention it. Don't invent one.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <div role="tabpanel" id="script-panel-6" aria-labelledby="script-tab-6" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">A follow-up</h3>
            <div class="prose">
              <p>Give it a few days, not a few hours. If they already said they need time, wait longer than that.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">One follow-up is usually enough</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>Hello [first name],

Just floating this back up in case it got buried. I'm still available to help with [the project], and happy to answer questions here in this thread.

If the timing isn't right, no worries at all.

[Your name]</pre>
            </div>
            <aside class="note">
              <p class="note-label">Note</p>
              <p>One follow-up is usually enough. No reply after that? Let it go and write the next proposal.</p>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="kit-section" id="look-for-adjacent-work-on-upwork">
        <h2>Look for adjacent work on Upwork</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Don't only search for your exact skill.</p>
          <p>Search the tools and platforms around it too.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>The job you can actually do is often posted under the software name. Not under the job title you had at work.</p>
        </aside>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>A few examples of how I think about this:</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
          <div class="tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Adjacent work examples">
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="adj-tab-1" aria-controls="adj-panel-1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">Newsletters</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="adj-tab-2" aria-controls="adj-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">HR</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="adj-tab-3" aria-controls="adj-panel-3" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Bookkeeping</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="adj-tab-4" aria-controls="adj-panel-4" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Drafting</button>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="adj-panel-1" aria-labelledby="adj-tab-1" class="is-active" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Newsletters</h3>
            <p>If you can help with newsletters, search for newsletter writing or setup. Then also search for people who need help setting up Mailchimp or Beehiiv.</p>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="adj-panel-2" aria-labelledby="adj-tab-2" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">HR</h3>
            <p>If you come from HR, search for HR work. Then also search for help with the platforms HR folks actually use.</p>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="adj-panel-3" aria-labelledby="adj-tab-3" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Bookkeeping</h3>
            <p>If you can do bookkeeping or finance, search for bookkeeper jobs. Then also search for jobs asking for QuickBooks or Xero help.</p>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="adj-panel-4" aria-labelledby="adj-tab-4" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Drafting</h3>
            <p>Me? I was a mechanical draftsman. So I could search for drafting work. I could also search for people who need help with SolidWorks or AutoCAD.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Years ago I helped an engineering department move from 2D AutoCAD to 3D SolidWorks. That experience has helped me win work since.</p>
          <p>The method is simple. Give yourself 20 minutes and make three short lists:</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="trio">
          <li>
            <span class="trio-num">1</span>
            <p>The work you already do. Newsletter setup. Google Ads. Drafting. HR support. Bookkeeping. Plain language.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="trio-num">2</span>
            <p>The tools and platforms you used to do it. Mailchimp. Beehiiv. SolidWorks. AutoCAD. QuickBooks. Xero. Whatever HR system you actually know.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="trio-num">3</span>
            <p>The people you used to help. Creators. Small manufacturers. An engineering team. An HR manager. A small-business owner.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Then go to Upwork, choose Jobs, and search each line, one at a time. Jot down how many posts come up, and whether you could honestly do that work. Keep the searches with real jobs you can do. Set aside the ones that are a stretch.</p>
          <p>You're not trying to become a new kind of freelancer overnight. You're just noticing the jobs that already sit next to the skills you have.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="kit-section" id="dont-shy-away-from-teach-me-jobs-on-upwork">
        <h2>Don't shy away from teach-me jobs on Upwork</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>A lot of freelancers skip posts where the client doesn't want to hire someone to do the work. They just want someone to teach them how.</p>
          <p>I wouldn't skip those.</p>
          <p>Several clients have hired me to teach them Google Ads at an hourly rate. Once we got into it, they often saw how much work it is, and how much you need to know to do it well.</p>
          <p>At that point, many of them decided they'd rather have me run it. Sometimes that turned into a longer project where I just manage it.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="pro-tip">
          <p class="pro-tip-label">
            <svg class="bulb" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path fill="currentColor" d="M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9v1zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7z"/></svg>
            Pro tip
          </p>
          <p>That's my experience, not a promise. A teaching job may never become a managed retainer for you, or pay a certain amount. Some people really do want to learn it and keep doing it themselves. That's a perfectly good outcome too.</p>
        </aside>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>If the post is clearly a teaching request, say so up front. If you're already on a call and they sound on the fence, offer both paths and let them choose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tabs" data-tabs>
          <div class="tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="Teach-me scripts">
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="teach-tab-1" aria-controls="teach-panel-1" aria-selected="true" tabindex="0">Teach them</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" id="teach-tab-2" aria-controls="teach-panel-2" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Take it over</button>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="teach-panel-1" aria-labelledby="teach-tab-1" class="is-active" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Pitching a teach-me engagement</h3>
            <div class="copy-block">
              <div class="ap-head">
                <p class="prompt-label">Say so up front if the post is a teaching request</p>
                <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
              </div>
              <pre>I can also teach you how to do this yourself, at an hourly rate, if that's what you want. We can work through [the task] together on Upwork calls, and I'll show you the parts I'd normally just go do.

Some people like having that option. Some decide, after a few sessions, that they'd rather have me run it. Either way is fine with me. We can start with a short teaching session and see how it feels.</pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div role="tabpanel" id="teach-panel-2" aria-labelledby="teach-tab-2" tabindex="0">
            <h3 class="tab-heading">Offering to take it over</h3>
